{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1517081364,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTIxNDYwMzM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2109","origin":"github"},"title":"install a specific version of a dataset","message":"#### What is the problem?\nATM we do not have AFAIK datalad way to install a specific version of a dataset. Although whenver it is a git-annex repo in indirect or v6 mode it should be trivial, direct mode makes it not so trivial, and with side-effects (just tried git annex proxy call and was left with bunch  of empty directories for the previous version)\n\nI though I had somewhere an issue for this but could not find.\nIt is a common convention to use `@` in url to point to a specific commitish, but I wonder if we should make it more explicit via url option to be handled on the client side (e.g., `///path/repo#version=commitish` and correspondingly with a regular url)\n\nrelated: #1671 - recursive checkout/merge","files":null}]}